__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.obcm
# ...except the small tile baked into the STM32 firmware via include_bytes! (issue
# #34). It must ship in-repo so the board crate builds without a separate pack step.
!firmware/obc-fw-stm32f429/tiles/*.obcm
# ...and the style presets' demo maps (B2, #899). They must ship in-repo: they are what
# a preset card on the hosted site renders, and baking one wants libGEOS, a 600 MB OSM
# extract and minutes of CPU — none of which belongs in a static-site deploy. Regenerate
# with builder/bake-previews.sh; the sizes are in previews.json beside them.
!builder/app/public/preview/*.obcm
# ...and the wasm assembly bridge's cell fixture (P4b, #1034), ~9 KB of baked OBCA cells. It must
# ship in-repo: it is the input half of the pin that says the browser's assembly is byte-identical
# to the native CLI's, asserted from both Rust and Node, and cutting it wants libGEOS. Regenerate
# with the two commands in apps/obc-web-assemble/tests/fixture.rs.
!apps/obc-web-assemble/tests/fixture/cells/**/*.obcm
*.obcr
# ...except the shared wire-protocol test vectors (S0, issue #268). They must ship
# in-repo: firmware `cargo test -p obc-vectors` and the app's swift tests pin their
# codecs to these exact bytes.
!specs/vectors/*.obcr
*.osm.pbf
# ...except the 735-byte hand-authored fixture the obc-pack ingest test reads
# (host/obc-pack `ingest::tests::tiny_truth_table`). It must ship in-repo so the
# test actually runs in CI — otherwise it silently reported PASS without ever running
# (issue #95). Source of truth is the committed tiny/tiny.osm; rebuild via
# builder/tests/corpus/build_corpus.sh.
!builder/tests/corpus/data/tiny.osm.pbf
# ...and the other two corpus fixtures, in-repo for the same reason: the POI
# end-to-end test (#422) and the 233-byte deliberately-unsorted file that pins
# `--bbox`'s refusal to crop a file whose ways precede their nodes (#910).
!builder/tests/corpus/data/poi.osm.pbf
!builder/tests/corpus/data/unsorted.osm.pbf
# ...and the two overlapping halves of tiny.osm that pin the native multi-`.pbf`
# merge (#920): ingesting the pair must reproduce ingesting the whole.
!builder/tests/corpus/data/tiny_west.osm.pbf
!builder/tests/corpus/data/tiny_east.osm.pbf
# The simulator's default route + track stores (its "SD card") — runtime artifacts.
# obc-sim resolves these relative to the working directory, which is the repo root now
# that the workspace is rooted here (`obc sim` runs cargo from $OBC_ROOT). Root-anchored
# so they only match the two stores, not a `routes/` anywhere else in the tree.
/routes/
/tracks/
*.obct
# ...except the shared recorded-track vector (A2, #896): the browser conversion bridge's
# byte-identity test reads it, so it must ship in-repo like the other protocol vectors.
!specs/vectors/*.obct
# The simulator's persisted-settings file (the device-RRAM stand-in) — a runtime artifact.
firmware/obc-settings.bin
# ui-snapshots.sh output — before/after PNG sweeps are per-branch scratch, never committed.
ui-snapshots/
.pytest_cache/
user_config.json
.worktrees/
# Claude Code's per-agent worktrees — real git worktrees, so `git add -A` would
# otherwise record one as a submodule gitlink and break every clone.
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
*.gpx
# ...except the deterministic source the protocol-vector route fixtures regenerate from.
!host/obc-vectors/src/route-source.gpx
# ...and the checked-in GPX export of the recorded-track vector (A2, #896) — the expected
# output the wasm bridge is compared against.
!specs/vectors/*.gpx
# ...and the iOS companion's bundled GPX import fixture (three OBCKit tests load it).
!companion-ios/Packages/OBCKit/Sources/OBCMock/Fixtures/sample-import.gpx
project/
# The wasm conversion bridge's build output (#896): `wasm-pack build` writes it into the
# frontend, `npm run build:wasm` rebuilds it, and CI builds it fresh on every run. wasm-pack
# drops its own `pkg/.gitignore` too — this entry is here so the intent is visible in one place.
builder/app/src/lib/convert/pkg/
# …and the assembly bridge's (#1034), the same way.
builder/app/src/lib/assemble/pkg/
# `obc` dev-task tooling (in tools/): personal defaults + the web builder's
# virtualenv + the optional local maps drop. The tooling itself (everything in
# tools/ except obc.local) is committed.
tools/obc.local
.venv/
/maps/
# Web builder frontend: dependencies + the Vite build output (CI builds it).
# The dev host builds into builder/server/static/dist/ (what the FastAPI server
# mounts); the static-web and desktop hosts into builder/app/dist/<host>/ — see
# #895. Both entries must keep matching vite.config.ts's outDirs: when they
# drifted apart, `npm run build` wrote to an unignored path and 640 KB of bundle
# got committed by accident (and the server mounted nothing).
builder/app/node_modules/
builder/app/dist/
builder/server/static/dist/
# The static tier's data files (#900): the Geofabrik index is ~1.7 MB of
# generated JSON that goes stale weekly, and the catalog manifest belongs to the
# bakery — both are produced at deploy time, never committed.
# `python -m builder.server.static_data --out <this dir>`
builder/app/public/data/

# XcodeBuildMCP session defaults (local tool state)
.xcodebuildmcp/

# Cargo build output — the workspace root now sits at the repo root (its members span
# firmware/, host/ and apps/), so the build dir is here rather than under firmware/.
target/
